<header><p class="enc-kicker">Religion / idea · deity</p><h1 class="enc-title">Artemis Pergaia</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Artemis of Perge</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/artemis">Artemis</a> Pergaia was the patron goddess of Perge in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pamphylia">Pamphylia</a>, a local deity identified with the Greek Artemis and called Wanassa Preiia, the 'Queen of Perge', in the Pamphylian dialect. Her rich temple stood near the city, and her cult image, a decorated conical stone, appears on the city's coins. The cult drew worshippers from across southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anatolia">Anatolia</a> in Hellenistic and Roman times.</p></div>
